{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function injectHotkeySequence(\n   sequence, \n   callback, \n   options?): void;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/angular-hotkeys/src/injectHotkeySequence.ts#L58","children":[{"type":"text","value":"injectHotkeySequence.ts:58"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Angular inject-based API for registering a keyboard shortcut sequence (Vim-style)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Allows you to register multi-key sequences like 'g g' or 'd d' that trigger\nwhen the full sequence is pressed within a timeout."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each step may include modifiers. You can chain the same modifier across\nsteps (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Shift+R"},{"type":"text","value":" then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Shift+T"},{"type":"text","value":"). Modifier-only keydown events (Shift,\nControl, Alt, or Meta pressed alone) are ignored while matching—they do not\nadvance the sequence or reset progress."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"sequence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"sequence"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeySequence"},{"type":"text","value":" | (() => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeySequence"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Array of hotkey strings that form the sequence (or getter function)"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"callback","children":[{"type":"text","value":"callback"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeyCallback"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Function to call when the sequence is completed"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"| "},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/InjectHotkeySequenceOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InjectHotkeySequenceOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n| (() => "},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/InjectHotkeySequenceOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InjectHotkeySequenceOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options for the sequence behavior (or getter function). "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enabled: false"},{"type":"text","value":" still registers\nthe sequence (visible in devtools); only execution is suppressed."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"@Component({ ... })\nexport class VimEditorComponent {\n  lastSequence = signal<string | null>(null)\n\n  constructor() {\n    injectHotkeySequence(['G', 'G'], () => this.lastSequence.set('gg → Go to top'))\n    injectHotkeySequence(['D', 'D'], () => this.lastSequence.set('dd → Delete line'))\n    injectHotkeySequence(['C', 'I', 'W'], () => this.lastSequence.set('ciw'), { timeout: 500 })\n    injectHotkeySequence(['Shift+R', 'Shift+T'], () => this.lastSequence.set('⇧R⇧T'))\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"sequence","text":"sequence","level":3},{"id":"callback","text":"callback","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction injectHotkeySequence(\n   sequence, \n   callback, \n   options?): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [injectHotkeySequence.ts:58](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/angular-hotkeys/src/injectHotkeySequence.ts#L58)\n\nAngular inject-based API for registering a keyboard shortcut sequence (Vim-style).\n\nAllows you to register multi-key sequences like 'g g' or 'd d' that trigger\nwhen the full sequence is pressed within a timeout.\n\nEach step may include modifiers. You can chain the same modifier across\nsteps (e.g. `Shift+R` then `Shift+T`). Modifier-only keydown events (Shift,\nControl, Alt, or Meta pressed alone) are ignored while matching—they do not\nadvance the sequence or reset progress.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### sequence\n\n`HotkeySequence` \\| (() => `HotkeySequence`)\n\nArray of hotkey strings that form the sequence (or getter function)\n\n### callback\n\n`HotkeyCallback`\n\nFunction to call when the sequence is completed\n\n### options?\n\n  \\| [`InjectHotkeySequenceOptions`](../interfaces/InjectHotkeySequenceOptions.md)\n  \\| (() => [`InjectHotkeySequenceOptions`](../interfaces/InjectHotkeySequenceOptions.md))\n\nOptions for the sequence behavior (or getter function). `enabled: false` still registers\n  the sequence (visible in devtools); only execution is suppressed.\n\n## Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\n@Component({ ... })\nexport class VimEditorComponent {\n  lastSequence = signal<string | null>(null)\n\n  constructor() {\n    injectHotkeySequence(['G', 'G'], () => this.lastSequence.set('gg → Go to top'))\n    injectHotkeySequence(['D', 'D'], () => this.lastSequence.set('dd → Delete line'))\n    injectHotkeySequence(['C', 'I', 'W'], () => this.lastSequence.set('ciw'), { timeout: 500 })\n    injectHotkeySequence(['Shift+R', 'Shift+T'], () => this.lastSequence.set('⇧R⇧T'))\n  }\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: injectHotkeySequence\ntitle: injectHotkeySequence\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction injectHotkeySequence(\n   sequence, \n   callback, \n   options?): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [injectHotkeySequence.ts:58](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/angular-hotkeys/src/injectHotkeySequence.ts#L58)\n\nAngular inject-based API for registering a keyboard shortcut sequence (Vim-style).\n\nAllows you to register multi-key sequences like 'g g' or 'd d' that trigger\nwhen the full sequence is pressed within a timeout.\n\nEach step may include modifiers. You can chain the same modifier across\nsteps (e.g. `Shift+R` then `Shift+T`). Modifier-only keydown events (Shift,\nControl, Alt, or Meta pressed alone) are ignored while matching—they do not\nadvance the sequence or reset progress.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### sequence\n\n`HotkeySequence` \\| (() => `HotkeySequence`)\n\nArray of hotkey strings that form the sequence (or getter function)\n\n### callback\n\n`HotkeyCallback`\n\nFunction to call when the sequence is completed\n\n### options?\n\n  \\| [`InjectHotkeySequenceOptions`](../interfaces/InjectHotkeySequenceOptions.md)\n  \\| (() => [`InjectHotkeySequenceOptions`](../interfaces/InjectHotkeySequenceOptions.md))\n\nOptions for the sequence behavior (or getter function). `enabled: false` still registers\n  the sequence (visible in devtools); only execution is suppressed.\n\n## Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\n@Component({ ... })\nexport class VimEditorComponent {\n  lastSequence = signal<string | null>(null)\n\n  constructor() {\n    injectHotkeySequence(['G', 'G'], () => this.lastSequence.set('gg → Go to top'))\n    injectHotkeySequence(['D', 'D'], () => this.lastSequence.set('dd → Delete line'))\n    injectHotkeySequence(['C', 'I', 'W'], () => this.lastSequence.set('ciw'), { timeout: 500 })\n    injectHotkeySequence(['Shift+R', 'Shift+T'], () => this.lastSequence.set('⇧R⇧T'))\n  }\n}\n```\n"}
